{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 14, :comments ["<b>And when you sell, etc.</b> According to its plain sense, as it sounds; and there is also a midrash: From where do we learn that when you sell, you must sell to your fellow Israelite? Scripture says, ״וְכִי תִמְכְּרוּ מִמְכָּר״ — sell to your fellow; and from where do we learn that if you come to buy, you must buy from your fellow Israelite? Scripture says, ״אוֹ קָנֹה״ — from the hand of your fellow (Sifra)." "<b>You shall not wrong.</b> This is monetary oppression (Bava Metzi'a 58)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:08:16.186608988Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}